F Derive                                          | Api/ChartPartition.h              | 123       | Cuts, flattens and arranges one sealed topology into its parametric domain. ExtentExhausted when the conditioning describes another revision or no scale packs The `SeamSpecification` is taken by const reference and its derived set is returned in the result rather than written into it, so a worker running this touches no document state at all. and re-flatten, recording the crossing edges as derived seams. `68` §4.1 prescribes it for a fold, and a chart with two boundary loops is the same failure one step earlier. Subdivision strictly reduces the face count and a single face is always a disc that flattens without folding, so it terminates. `68` §7 puts this on `34`'s `Background` class; called on the tick it would stall a stroke.
